WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.390
Warm an enzyme and its substrate,
and the reaction speeds up.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:09.080
Keep warming, and past a certain
point the rate drops steeply.

3
00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:13.460
Many human enzymes work best
near 37 degrees Celsius.

4
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:18.230
But an enzyme from a hot-spring
bacterium works best near 75.

5
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.000
So why does warming an enzyme speed it up,

6
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.700
until suddenly it hardly works at all?

7
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.370
In this mission, you'll measure
a reaction's rate from a curve,

8
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.230
using a tangent drawn at the very start.

9
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:35.030
Then you'll see how pH and the amount
of substrate change the rate too.

10
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.070
Your mission: explain why
warming an enzyme speeds it up,

11
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.560
until suddenly it hardly works at all.
